From: Hector Bujanda <hector.bujanda@digi.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 09:39:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ccimx95: reserve gpio1_15 for SM (secure) to handle
 WDOG_ANY

https://onedigi.atlassian.net/browse/DEL-10136

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [DEY specific]

Signed-off-by: Hector Bujanda <hector.bujanda@digi.com>
---
 plat/imx/imx9/common/imx9_bl31_setup.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/imx/imx9/common/imx9_bl31_setup.c b/plat/imx/imx9/common/imx9_bl31_setup.c
index 55bd95cea..445c40749 100644
--- a/plat/imx/imx9/common/imx9_bl31_setup.c
+++ b/plat/imx/imx9/common/imx9_bl31_setup.c
@@ -115,10 +115,10 @@ void bl31_plat_arch_setup(void)
 #if defined(PLAT_imx95)
 	/*
 	 * The code above does not handle GPIO1.
-	 * Assign all the GPIO1 pins but GPIO1_10 to non-secure world
+	 * Assign all the GPIO1 pins but GPIO1_10 and GPIO1_15 to non-secure world
 	 */
-	mmio_write_32(GPIO1_BASE + 0x18, 0xfffffbff);
-	mmio_write_32(GPIO1_BASE + 0x10, 0xfffffbff);
+	mmio_write_32(GPIO1_BASE + 0x18, 0xffff7bff);
+	mmio_write_32(GPIO1_BASE + 0x10, 0xffff7bff);
 
 	/*
 	 * Route GPIO1 interrupt lines as follows:


